<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Surrey</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 700 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Saxon territory south of the Thames whose name, the 'southern district', survives as the county of Surrey.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Surrey, Suthrige, probably began as the southern part of a larger Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> territory on both sides of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-thames">Thames</a>. In the 7th century it lay between Kent, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wessex">Wessex</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-sussex">Sussex</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a> and was ruled by local leaders under one or another of them.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The only known ruler is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frithuwold">Frithuwold</a>, a sub-king under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wulfhere-of-mercia">Wulfhere</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Kingdom of Mercia</a>, who around 672 to 674 endowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chertsey-abbey">Chertsey Abbey</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eorcenwald">Eorcenwald</a>. The charter shows estates, minsters and Mercian overlordship but no independent dynasty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Surrey never had a lasting royal line. Control passed between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wessex">Wessex</a>, and in the 9th century it became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">West Saxon</a> shire, keeping its name and much of its boundary.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-surrey.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Surrey" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Des Blenkinsopp · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edge_of_the_North_Downs_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7610138.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 700 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frithuwold</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Surrey, Suthrige</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=650&amp;focus=kingdom-of-surrey" aria-label="Kingdom of Surrey on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4670 402 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Surrey lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4990 658L4962 619M4990 658L4970 663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4962 619h0M4970 663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4990 658h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4990 658h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=650&amp;focus=kingdom-of-surrey">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
